{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Ramaṇīyakuṭika","html":"<article id='thag1.58'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.58 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.58 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Chaṭṭhavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Six </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ramaṇīyakuṭikattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ramaṇīyakuṭika </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ramaṇīyā me kuṭikā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>My hut is pleasing, delightful, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saddhādeyyā manoramā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a gift given in faith. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na me attho kumārīhi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve no need of girls: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ attho tahiṁ gacchatha nāriyo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go, ladies, to those in need! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Ramaṇīyakuṭiko thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
